WHAT CHANGED
- memorian-run-retention.ts: writeMemorianRunOutcome writes <runDir>/outcome.json
  (version 1, runId, status, cause?, nudged, finishedAt) mode 0o600, best-effort warn.
  pruneMemorianRuns ages <recallDir>/runs by newest inner file mtime; missing/unparseable
  outcome.json uses 7d; non-empty nudged or status "failed" uses 30d; rename to .prune-<name>
  then remove; leftover .prune-* tombstones swept; ENOENT tolerated.
  createThrottledPrune is fire-and-forget, hourly .last-prune marker, in-flight coalesce.
- memorian-judge-run.ts: writeMemorianRunOutcome at every terminal classification
  (completed / completed+partial salvage / failed deadline|child_failed|session_create_failed
  / dropped cancelled) with accepted nudge paths. candidates.json and transcript-window.txt
  untouched.
- wiring-memorian.ts: one throttled prune per composition keyed by identity recall dir;
  wrap trigger.onSettled so prune fires after trigger capture. memorian-trigger.ts untouched.
- memorian-runner.ts: line-17 comment now describes retention (one sentence). No config keys.

TDD: tests written first, RED captured, then implementation, GREEN captured.

